WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.469
The final days before the Iowa caucuses

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.503
as the Republican front

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.539
runner is packing up his personal 757

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.474
and leaving the state

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.708
because Donald Trump

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.176
opting for sitting in court

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.911
rather than going to speak

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:12.912
to voters and campaign

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.314
in front of them tomorrow,

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.082
that is something he is choosing to do.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:16.649
Option.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.384
We will speak about that,

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.985
the lawyer later in the hour.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.420
But that comes as his two leading

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.888
challengers are begging for

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:24.891
votes, is also battling each other.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:25.825
Also, meanwhile,

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:26.559
President Biden

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.861
today was in South Carolina,

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:28.528
making it clear

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.030
who he expects

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.097
to be facing

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:35.368
as the Republican nominee come November.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.103
We saw something on January six

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.371
we had never seen before,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.707
even during the Civil War.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.675
Insurrectionists waving Confederate flags

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.310
inside the halls of Congress

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.346
built by enslaved Americans.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.647
For hours,

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.815
the defeated former president

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.083
sat in a private dining room

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.352
off of my half of the Oval Office

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.421
and did nothing. Nothing.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.622
Absolutely nothing.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.924
Losers are taught to concede

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.926
when they lose.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:04.731
He's a loser.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.433
No holding back there in that speech.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.634
I'm joined tonight by former

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:08.701
Republican Congressman

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.770
Adam Kinzinger and former Obama

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.539
administration official Van Jones.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.641
Thank you both for being here tonight.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.008
And, Van,

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:15.341
you know,

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.509
there was this one line

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.410
from President Biden.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.578
You know, he's in South Carolina.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.780
He's attempting to rally black voters

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.881
and he's been losing support

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.616
with them in the state that helped really

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.417
propel him

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.586
to the nomination back in 2020.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.888
But he drew this direct line at one point

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:29.489
during the speech.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.124
And I want everyone to listen to this.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.860
Between this history of white supremacy

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.961
to what the former president

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.964
is doing today,

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.399
in our time,

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.034
there's still the old ghost

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:44.237
of new government, a new government.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.940
We all need to rise to meet the moment,

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:50.043
the moment is now.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:50.677
I mean, Ben,

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:51.644
what did you make of him

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.780
essentially arguing that, you know, this

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.381
those who say the Confederate rebellion

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.583
was this noble cause,

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.851
that it was self-serving,

00:01:57.851 --> 00:02:00.120
as Biden was putting it in the same way

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.721
that he says Trump is rewriting history

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:03.289
by trying to falsely claim

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.792
that the election was stolen?

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:06.693
Yeah, you know,

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.293
I thought it was

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.461
actually pretty powerful.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.496
It wasn't a frame

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.798
I thought of before I heard before,

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.366
you know, the lost cause,

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.701
You know, that's sort of the

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.902
I grew up in Tennessee.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.570
You know, some of us are Southerners and,

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.872
you know, that kind of,

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:22.442
you know, we we have this lost cause.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.276
And you look back

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.210
and you go back

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.512
over and over and over again,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.247
and this is like a second lost

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:29.349
cause is like what Biden is saying,

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:30.350
that the Southern Confederates

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:30.850
were defeated

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.152
and they would never admit it.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.020
And now you've got the Trump

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.955
machine defeated and it won't admit it.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.323
And he's drawing a line

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.325
between that refusal

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.660
to deal with reality

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.663
and the violence of of, you know, January

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.565
the seventh and January six

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.233
and the potential violence

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.301
that could come with this election.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:51.371
So for me, I think he's doing a good job

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.940
trying to get back to his home turf,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.807
South Carolina,

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.209
get back to the black base,

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.011
reminding them of some of the stuff

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.279
that maybe people have forgotten about

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.113
and reframing

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:00.980
what we're seeing

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:01.681
as a part

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.183
of a long tradition

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:03.750
of very,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.119
very dangerous politics in America.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.353
And Congressman Kinzinger,

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.122
I mean, this comes as Elise

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.090
Stefanik yesterday on the Sunday shows.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.059
She is the Republican conference chair,

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.628
and she's now echoing the language

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:16.829
that the former president is using

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:17.430
when it comes

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.032
to the January six defendants,

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.867
the people who went to the Capitol

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.202
and rioted that day,

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.970
describing them as hostages.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.273
This is what she said on Meet the Press.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:27.840
I have

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.042
concerns about the

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:32.011
treatment of January six hostages.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.946
I have concerns.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:35.315
We have a role in Congress of oversight

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.350
over our treatment of prisoners.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.251
And I believe that

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.886
we're seeing the weaponization

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.154
of the federal government

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.156
against not just President Trump,

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:43.790
but we're seeing it

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.959
against conservatives.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.060
What did you make,

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.127
Congressman, of seeing

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:51.497
such a prominent member of your party

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:54.067
saying that?

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:58.037
Well, I mean, Elise is so incredibly,

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:01.574
insanely thirsty to be vice president.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.775
I mean, that's what she's doing.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:03.843
She's out there

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.546
mimicking what Donald Trump says.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.780
He knows he's watching

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.315
and he probably center attacks,

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.017
told her good job, Elise.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.219
And she felt really good about herself.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.420
I mean, that's what she's doing

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:14.954
and she's doing it.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.489
And this is a look,

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:17.557
if I'm a rank and file

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.225
member of the House still, here's

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.660
where I would be upset,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.929
because I used to be able to just say,

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.063
oh, Donald Trump,

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.231
you know, I don't know what he says.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.332
I'm not paying attention.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.869
You now have the leader of the

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.071
messaging branch,

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.207
what you say as a Republican.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.009
The conference chair comes up

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:36.843
talking points

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.946
now saying there, January six hostages.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.014
Here's what you're going to see.

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:41.848
Caitlin,

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.883
this is now going to be echoed over

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:44.817
and over

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.686
as it becomes a litmus test,

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:47.553
whether you're a true

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.022
conservative or not,

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:51.424
whether you say hostages or prisoners,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.892
and soon you're going to see more

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.093
and more people saying this.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.362
I think it's so obvious.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.031
It's just one of the areas,

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:58.464
I think,

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.933
as well as Joe Biden did in that speech,

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:01.734
one of the areas

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:02.969
I think he really needs to push

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:03.736
even harder on

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.071
is there's this idea

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.873
that Donald Trump is a tough person

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.741
who's doing this authoritarian things

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.043
because he's strong.

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:13.012
The reality is he's a he's he's a whiner.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.682
He's frightened, He's scared.

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.516
He's doing this

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.451
because he's a victim in his own mind

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.419
and he wants to convince

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.887
everybody he's a victim.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:21.688
Donald Trump

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:24.490
